(1085002, 130651, 17507, '<td valign="top">I think the soft focus works really well for this image. It enhances the rustic feeling. Unfortunately, voters on this site almost exclusively prefer crisp focus, so I doubt this will be getting as high a score as it should.</td>', 'I think the soft focus works really well for this image. It enhances the rustic feeling. Unfortunately, voters on this site almost exclusively prefer crisp focus, so I doubt this will be getting as high a score as it should.', '2004-12-31 22:54:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1085003, 130201, 17507, '<td valign="top">Rotate the spedometer 180 or 200 degrees, and then you''ll have a killer photograph :)<br/>The mileage (kilometerage?) indicator is a nice subtlety of this picture.</td>', 'Rotate the spedometer 180 or 200 degrees, and then you''ll have a killer photograph :)The mileage (kilometerage?) indicator is a nice subtlety of this picture.', '2004-12-31 22:55:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1085004, 130812, 17507, '<td valign="top">By the fact that it''s the only element in the picture that''s in color, I take it that you meant the rusty hinge to be the focal point of the composition. If so, it''s generally better to have the FP farther from the border of the image, lest too much of the image become dead space distracting from the focus.</td>', 'By the fact that it''s the only element in the picture that''s in color, I take it that you meant the rusty hinge to be the focal point of the composition. If so, it''s generally better to have the FP farther from the border of the image, lest too much of the image become dead space distracting from the focus.', '2004-12-31 22:56:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1085006, 130822, 17507, '<td valign="top">it''s a shame the focus is on the table and not on the pencil...</td>', 'it''s a shame the focus is on the table and not on the pencil...', '2004-12-31 22:58:59.000000', NULL, 1),
