(1092483, 131267, 30552, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments. I really enjoyed reading them.<br/> <br/>The photo is not really a X-ray.<br/> <br/>I took the baitcaster (fishing reel) and removed the side plate. <br/>I then removed the spool from the inside so I could see the gears.<br/> <br/>I set the shot up. Turned the lights off.<br/>The room was pitch black. I set the camera self timer. The shutter opened for 6 seconds. <br/> <br/>Then I took a manual flash that I just held in my hand and flashed the reel from one side. Then I removed the side plate from the baitcaster and flashed it from the other side. All before the shutter closed.<br/> <br/>I used paint shop pro 8 one step photo fix to auto adjust color and sharpness.<br/> <br/>Then I used the "Negative Image" button to get what you see now.<br/> <br/>I did try to place it on a diagonal as I thought it would look better with the fishing rod, but I just could not seem to make it work without the reel being so much smaller looking in the photo.<br/> <br/>I took about 8 photo''s of the reel and this one turned out the closest to what I had in mind.<br/> <br/>There are a number of things I would do different next time for a photo like this.<br/> <br/>I''m very happy with my 61st place being this is my first challenge.<br/> <br/>Thanks again,</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments. I really enjoyed reading them. The photo is not really a X-ray. I took the baitcaster (fishing reel) and removed the side plate. I then removed the spool from the inside so I could see the gears. I set the shot up. Turned the lights off.The room was pitch black. I set the camera self timer. The shutter opened for 6 seconds.  Then I took a manual flash that I just held in my hand and flashed the reel from one side. Then I removed the side plate from the baitcaster and flashed it from the other side. All before the shutter closed. I used paint shop pro 8 one step photo fix to auto adjust color and sharpness. Then I used the "Negative Image" button to get what you see now. I did try to place it on a diagonal as I thought it would look better with the fishing rod, but I just could not seem to make it work without the reel being so much smaller looking in the photo. I took about 8 photo''s of the reel and this one turned out the closest to what I had in mind. There are a number of things I would do different next time for a photo like this. I''m very happy with my 61st place being this is my first challenge. Thanks again,', '2005-01-05 08:41:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1092484, 131173, 30251, '<td valign="top">Hey thanks for the views, votes, and comments, to all of those who are wondering this is an antique sausage grinder. I did feel having this much out of focus would either make this unique and beautiful of hard to look at.<br/> <br/>I shot a few other angles, but I didn''t think that any of them met the challenge. <br/>i.e.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=133561" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30251/thumb/133561.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30251/thumb/133561.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30251/thumb/133561.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Hey thanks for the views, votes, and comments, to all of those who are wondering this is an antique sausage grinder. I did feel having this much out of focus would either make this unique and beautiful of hard to look at. I shot a few other angles, but I didn''t think that any of them met the challenge. i.e.', '2005-01-05 08:42:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1092508, 130995, 24467, '<td valign="top">Very, very thanks all for the kind words and for appreciating.<br/> <br/>I did this image , and the title with a purpose of expressing my sinceres wishes for all peolpe of this site and whole community, who contributes for this successful, and beloved space.<br/> <br/>Receiving an Ribbon, AND an Blue, was more than I expected, and this is really an great year´s beginning for me.<br/> <br/>So, Happy 2005! Peace, Love, Health! and for DPC participators: Ribbons!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-01-05 09:04:19.</i></td>', 'Very, very thanks all for the kind words and for appreciating. I did this image , and the title with a purpose of expressing my sinceres wishes for all peolpe of this site and whole community, who contributes for this successful, and beloved space. Receiving an Ribbon, AND an Blue, was more than I expected, and this is really an great year´s beginning for me. So, Happy 2005! Peace, Love, Health! and for DPC participators: Ribbons!', '2005-01-05 09:02:50.000000', '2005-01-05 09:04:19.000000', 0),
(1092514, 131277, 20679, '<td valign="top">Wow - my first top 20 finish. Good way to start the new year. I''m hoping for a top 10 before the end of 2005.</td>', 'Wow - my first top 20 finish. Good way to start the new year. I''m hoping for a top 10 before the end of 2005.', '2005-01-05 09:05:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1092542, 130995, 24467, '<td valign="top">About the technical:<br/> <br/>To manage the timing , an electronic sound activated device was used to trigger the flash. It is an simple homemade circuit.<br/> <br/>To control the light is more difficult, as splashs are unpredictables, I tried to put white reflectors everywhere possible. An black background was  positioned one meter far.  <br/> <br/>As champagne was expensive, an cheaper substitute was used. Sorry for this non glamourous true.<br/> <br/>Thanks all again.<br/> <br/>Edited: About the tries, I did an set of 25 shots, went to the computer an analyze at the monitor. As none was good, I did another set of 25, which produced 3 good images. I think I selected the best one.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-04-11 11:13:05.</i></td>', 'About the technical: To manage the timing , an electronic sound activated device was used to trigger the flash. It is an simple homemade circuit. To control the light is more difficult, as splashs are unpredictables, I tried to put white reflectors everywhere possible. An black background was  positioned one meter far.   As champagne was expensive, an cheaper substitute was used. Sorry for this non glamourous true. Thanks all again. Edited: About the tries, I did an set of 25 shots, went to the computer an analyze at the monitor. As none was good, I did another set of 25, which produced 3 good images. I think I selected the best one.', '2005-01-05 09:23:42.000000', '2005-04-11 12:13:05.000000', 0),
(1092553, 130811, 10047, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by geewhy:</b></div><hr/><i> I expected this to do so much better..it deserved to in my opinion. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Geewhy. I thought it would do better also. It was interesting that it it received so many comments for the high end of the mid-packers. It was one of those photos which I liked, but had second thoughts about submitting it because my taste isn''t always mainstream. Thanks again.</td>', 'Originally posted by geewhy: I expected this to do so much better..it deserved to in my opinion.   Thanks Geewhy. I thought it would do better also. It was interesting that it it received so many comments for the high end of the mid-packers. It was one of those photos which I liked, but had second thoughts about submitting it because my taste isn''t always mainstream. Thanks again.', '2005-01-05 09:31:39.000000', NULL, 0),
